🔔**A fire alarm with a GSM module saved a woman**

In the Bashkirian city of Blagoveshchensk, a group I visually impaired woman put a kettle on the stove and forgot about it. The device was triggered and alerted the homeowner to the danger.

In Bashkortostan, the authorities have begun installing such alarms. In total, more than 1,300 alarms will be installed in homes where people with limited mobility and people with hearing and visual impairments live. The GSM module makes it possible to automatically transmit a signal to several recipients:  
⭕emergency services;  
⭕guardianship authorities;  
⭕the village council;  
⭕relatives, etc.

__The head of Russia’s EMERCOM, Alexander Kurenkov, noted the necessity of such work.__

“Our task is to reduce the number of fatalities. We are fighting for human lives; a comprehensive approach is important here. It is necessary to extend this experience to other regions as well,” Alexander Kurenkov stressed.

